<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch12-chapter-ht-compare-means" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Comparing Groups - Quantitative Response</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> This chapter begins with a lesson on summarizing data when you have one categorical and one quantitative variable. 
      Then students learn how to perform a simulation-based hypothesis tests/randomization tests for comparing population means. 
      We begin with a comparison of two groups and extend this to any number of groups. 
      Students will learn when a cause-and-effect conclusion can be drawn and the importance of study design.
      We also look at the special case of paired data. 
    </p>
  </introduction>

